    "title": "Injured AEW Star Backstage At Dynamite-Collision Tapings - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sap Sinha ,\n1 hours ago\nAEW fans have wondered about Penelope Ford for a long time, and now they finally got a small clue about her whereabouts.\nPwinsider is reporting that Ford was seen backstage at the October 14 episode of Dynamite, although nobody has confirmed whether she is close to returning to the ring.\nFord is still out with an injury, and it’s unclear what she was doing at Wednesday’s tapings.\nFord has been away since February 25, when she injured her ankle on Dynamite in Denver. She and Megan Bayne were facing Willow Nightingale and Harley Cameron for the AEW Women’s World Tag Team Championship. After a moonsault to the outside, she landed on her feet, tried to keep going, and then had to leave as the pain grew, so AEW changed the finish on the spot.\nBryan Alvarez later reported a sprained ankle, which sounded like a short absence, yet she has been sidelined for months.",
    "summary": "AEW fans have wondered about Penelope Ford for a long time, and now they finally got a small clue about her whereabouts. Pwinsider is reporting that Ford was seen backstage at the October 14 episode of Dynamite, although nobody has confirmed whether she is close to returning to the ring. She and Megan Bayne were facing Willow Nightingale and Harley Cameron for the AEW Women’s World Tag Team Championship.",
